<title>THAILAND: Thai industrial park developer cut IPO price.</title>
<headline>Thai industrial park developer cut IPO price.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai industrial park developer Bangkok Pakong Industrial Park 2 Plc said on Wednesday it had cut the initial public offering price of its 21.7 million new shares to 18 baht ($0.70) from 20 baht previously announced.</p>
<p>The reduction in IPO price was due to the company's attempt to attract retail investors for the share subscription because of a bearish mood prevailing in the stock market, its president Vikrom Kromadit told a news conference.</p>
<p>Bangkok Pakong is scheduled to make a public offering of its new shares between June 11-13.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
